  "location_review": {
    "01-return": "Gipath Sands: original coastal Jun ruins and bridges; deliberate sea-facing view, no visible hero.",
    "02-gipath": "Middle Mountains: native green dragon valley; no introduced creature and no visible hero.",
    "03-ingos": "Lake and castle in the original Ingos map; explicitly retained scenic exception.",
    "04-suslanger": "Later Suslanger city map gz18h: irrigation canals and orchards. Not the prison camp or Rindale arrival hub.",
    "05-astral": "Late Jigran map gz35j: Sadrok island bridges, statue and Firez fortress skyline. Native expansion text identifies this as the Hadagan stronghold.",
    "06-hdlands": "Dead City ruined fountain and paving in gz9g. Actual HD Lands 1.5.0 package; credit Atom.",
    "08-tactical": "Original orc, white wolf and witch encounter in Sands, original MOB positions; Gipath shop-1 leather and stone equipment.",
    "09-first": "Native white tiger in Ingos gz11k, NID 3990; iron bow and Kania armour. Track the living opponent with normal direct-control input.",
    "10-third": "Native OgreHadaganF15, NID 150993, outside later Suslanger city gz18h. Zak is free after the prison/catacomb escape; Hadagan steel equipment is available through the Suslanger shop-4 catalogue. gz15h prison footage is rejected.",
    "11-coop": "Two actual network players at the Dead City fountain approach, with Gipath equipment.",
    "14-touch": "Sands bridge encounter area with native touch controls and Gipath equipment.",
    "15-gamepad": "Dead City fountain approach with native pie-section system wheel and Gipath equipment.",
    "16-play": "Late-map establishing view behind the platform/website end card.",
    "17-rain-tactical": "Archived ravine take; excluded from revision 2 because the rock walls dominate the battle composition.",
    "18-ogre-third": "Original later Suslanger ogre; stationary player attack input avoids repeated approach nudges.",
    "19-ogre-tactical": "Archived isometric ogre angle; excluded from revision 2 because palm fronds obscure the action.",
    "20-tiger-first": "Longer native Ingos white tiger encounter, tracked from first-person eyes.",
    "21-rain-ruins": "Later Gipath coastal Jun ruins, native zone rain.",
    "22-endcard": "Later Lost in Astral Sadrok island and fortress.",
    "23-dead-city": "Original Dead City skeletons 2304, 1584 and 1585, retained at their authored positions; player approaches from the open ground east of the ruined fountain. Native rain, HD Lands, Gipath leather/stone wardrobe, and a player-craftable fireball with effect/stamina runes.",
    "24-dragon-valley": "Original Middle Mountains dragonkin 1434/1435 and flying green dragon 1436; player remains on the valley path, with the camera raised to include the dragon above the ruins. Native actor statistics and Gipath equipment/spell components.",
    "26-lava-first": "Rejected from the final edit: the tunnel camera obscured the setting; the earlier source is retained only for reference.",
    "27-orcs-first": "Original orc camp by the Big Lake, gz7g, NID 5226. West-side player approach keeps the lake, bridge and original ogre behind the melee; Gipath leather and granite sword.",
    "28-banshee-first": "Two Rivers, Lost in Astral gz34j: native banshee fighter NID 44453163 beside the river. Kania steel kit, actual first-person sword swings and native banshee attacks.",
    "29-troll-third": "Original Ingos blue troll, NID 4043, approached from the east along the snow path. Kania iron and blue-troll-hide kit. The alternative south-facing angle was rejected because its foreground cliff blocks the view.",
    "30-portal-third": "The guarded Portal, later Suslanger map gz19h (not prison gz15h). Original gate guards 997003 and 997007, player approaches from the northeast; the gate towers and courtyard frame the duel. Hadagan steel equipment fits the free, later-campaign Zak.",
    "31-fortress-third": "Dar-Ulgorn fortress, native guard 44453161 beside the canal bridge. The east bank approach at 201.25,99.25 has a clear camera, visible bridge and reflections, and a native walkable path. A continuous one-second forward input precedes combat; offline capture keeps the normal input watchdog alive. West approaches were rejected for bridge-post, roof and shrub obstructions.",
    "25-touch-city": "Native touch menu in the Dead City, with Gipath equipment.",
    "32-dragon-first": "Island of Death, Lost in Astral gz32j: native red dragon 44432950 flying over the sea beside the island bridge. Player stands on the island road at the bridge landing, with Kania steel and a long crossbow. The offshore blue-dragon angle was rejected."
  },
